"answer-6866f740-c6c6-5a04-9ec8-25e5e19817c8" "answer-001907a0-d758-52f3-b5d8-ac5e8cf1f77e" "answer-df9cb88c-fbc1-50f3-a483-943aeb28c2c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7387e8a-9279-5e09-a846-740afcb713d4" :answer/id #uuid "d7387e8a-9279-5e09-a846-740afcb713d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Null}(A)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c534e011-9779-5c08-bf91-332ae2ca87d4" :answer/id #uuid "c534e011-9779-5c08-bf91-332ae2ca87d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Null}({A}^{-1})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6866f740-c6c6-5a04-9ec8-25e5e19817c8" :answer/id #uuid "6866f740-c6c6-5a04-9ec8-25e5e19817c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{span}(A)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-001907a0-d758-52f3-b5d8-ac5e8cf1f77e" :answer/id #uuid "001907a0-d758-52f3-b5d8-ac5e8cf1f77e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "det(A)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df9cb88c-fbc1-50f3-a483-943aeb28c2c8" :answer/id #uuid "df9cb88c-fbc1-50f3-a483-943aeb28c2c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "det({A}^{-1})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-007b2eff-be4f-5ff5-af75-29d7ce49d108" :question/id #uuid "007b2eff-be4f-5ff5-af75-29d7ce49d108" :question/math-academy-id "q-141201" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and  $\\text{rank}(A)=4?$ \n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)=\\{0\\}$\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. By the invertible matrix theorem,  $A$ is an invertible matrix because $\\text{rank}(A)=4.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $A$ is invertible, it must be $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. By the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$ because $A$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1b91479d-fc9f-5493-8022-99b07638d6b0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1b91479d-fc9f-5493-8022-99b07638d6b0" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b91479d-fc9f-5493-8022-99b07638d6b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-07ea5ae9-a33a-5951-9b11-5dc1678ec0ec" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a01f5c26-889c-59f3-aea4-5b800234178a" "answer-07ea5ae9-a33a-5951-9b11-5dc1678ec0ec" "answer-2dee1bb0-b584-5a13-acb7-dbc8b8f98b95" "answer-c6fd3f74-8d86-59d5-969d-0f73063566e3" "answer-f1a5d0c5-12bc-5492-a130-1c6bfb4dadcf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a01f5c26-889c-59f3-aea4-5b800234178a" :answer/id #uuid "a01f5c26-889c-59f3-aea4-5b800234178a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07ea5ae9-a33a-5951-9b11-5dc1678ec0ec" :answer/id #uuid "07ea5ae9-a33a-5951-9b11-5dc1678ec0ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2dee1bb0-b584-5a13-acb7-dbc8b8f98b95" :answer/id #uuid "2dee1bb0-b584-5a13-acb7-dbc8b8f98b95" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6fd3f74-8d86-59d5-969d-0f73063566e3" :answer/id #uuid "c6fd3f74-8d86-59d5-969d-0f73063566e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1a5d0c5-12bc-5492-a130-1c6bfb4dadcf" :answer/id #uuid "f1a5d0c5-12bc-5492-a130-1c6bfb4dadcf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-40fb1ecb-b40f-5f25-b77a-57f70d15c44b" :question/id #uuid "40fb1ecb-b40f-5f25-b77a-57f70d15c44b" :question/math-academy-id "q-141198" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and  $det(A)=0?$ \n\nI. $A$ is not invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5$\n\nIII. $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col)}(A)=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null)}(A)=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. A matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=0,$ our matrix $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{rank}(A)=5.$\nSince $A$ is not invertible, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible,  it must be $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c78aa62f-0e43-5933-85ca-b11f30121e9d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c78aa62f-0e43-5933-85ca-b11f30121e9d" :answer-field/id #uuid "c78aa62f-0e43-5933-85ca-b11f30121e9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8385037e-b7cf-5ce8-80e7-5480da9f4742" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8385037e-b7cf-5ce8-80e7-5480da9f4742" "answer-83819081-3ffe-5b21-ac5b-ef6bd26bb168" "answer-86f2e9f4-3420-54d6-a57c-2966d7bea624" "answer-f453a8ad-b614-59d8-8bdc-cf9373db8c89" "answer-a8dd8b94-5449-5e15-bbed-68d5ef48c3ca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8385037e-b7cf-5ce8-80e7-5480da9f4742" :answer/id #uuid "8385037e-b7cf-5ce8-80e7-5480da9f4742" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83819081-3ffe-5b21-ac5b-ef6bd26bb168" :answer/id #uuid "83819081-3ffe-5b21-ac5b-ef6bd26bb168" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86f2e9f4-3420-54d6-a57c-2966d7bea624" :answer/id #uuid "86f2e9f4-3420-54d6-a57c-2966d7bea624" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f453a8ad-b614-59d8-8bdc-cf9373db8c89" :answer/id #uuid "f453a8ad-b614-59d8-8bdc-cf9373db8c89" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8dd8b94-5449-5e15-bbed-68d5ef48c3ca" :answer/id #uuid "a8dd8b94-5449-5e15-bbed-68d5ef48c3ca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0a0c9232-89fc-57dc-83d9-632995f2a765" :question/id #uuid "0a0c9232-89fc-57dc-83d9-632995f2a765" :question/math-academy-id "q-34929" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-65a8a987-b1f9-5fda-b11d-202fd35c0139"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-65a8a987-b1f9-5fda-b11d-202fd35c0139" :answer-field/id #uuid "65a8a987-b1f9-5fda-b11d-202fd35c0139" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6a0d3e4b-0e93-59fe-9cf9-ff2f7de1a3e7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fe7d54d8-0b88-5b60-9559-438bba9408ef" "answer-6a0d3e4b-0e93-59fe-9cf9-ff2f7de1a3e7" "answer-f63ddbaf-3159-5f89-a08c-517e465848a1" "answer-5602a65b-5713-5ed2-bdd4-7c2a89efe1f3" "answer-8d75866b-a6fe-5c0e-8c96-11f1e0e723da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe7d54d8-0b88-5b60-9559-438bba9408ef" :answer/id #uuid "fe7d54d8-0b88-5b60-9559-438bba9408ef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a0d3e4b-0e93-59fe-9cf9-ff2f7de1a3e7" :answer/id #uuid "6a0d3e4b-0e93-59fe-9cf9-ff2f7de1a3e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f63ddbaf-3159-5f89-a08c-517e465848a1" :answer/id #uuid "f63ddbaf-3159-5f89-a08c-517e465848a1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5602a65b-5713-5ed2-bdd4-7c2a89efe1f3" :answer/id #uuid "5602a65b-5713-5ed2-bdd4-7c2a89efe1f3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d75866b-a6fe-5c0e-8c96-11f1e0e723da" :answer/id #uuid "8d75866b-a6fe-5c0e-8c96-11f1e0e723da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186272347 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{rank}(A)<4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4,$ or equivalently $\\text{rank}(A)<4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-66aeec20-f33b-58e9-909c-e866d7b79c69" :question/id #uuid "66aeec20-f33b-58e9-909c-e866d7b79c69" :question/math-academy-id "q-141196" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-33cd506b-d09b-50d0-b353-d0e67be14e46"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-33cd506b-d09b-50d0-b353-d0e67be14e46" :answer-field/id #uuid "33cd506b-d09b-50d0-b353-d0e67be14e46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-22d4c374-6702-575a-adef-908f42b74c37" :answer-field/choices ["answer-76cde27a-9ace-54a5-8396-92267ce3cc46" "answer-22d4c374-6702-575a-adef-908f42b74c37" "answer-9adf27f7-10ea-578a-a1d6-83396d7db9c6" "answer-f97850ab-a157-554f-a1df-1ca38933ab0b" "answer-f550b866-e3d0-5255-9950-2dbd691d15a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76cde27a-9ace-54a5-8396-92267ce3cc46" :answer/id #uuid "76cde27a-9ace-54a5-8396-92267ce3cc46" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22d4c374-6702-575a-adef-908f42b74c37" :answer/id #uuid "22d4c374-6702-575a-adef-908f42b74c37" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9adf27f7-10ea-578a-a1d6-83396d7db9c6" :answer/id #uuid "9adf27f7-10ea-578a-a1d6-83396d7db9c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f97850ab-a157-554f-a1df-1ca38933ab0b" :answer/id #uuid "f97850ab-a157-554f-a1df-1ca38933ab0b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f550b866-e3d0-5255-9950-2dbd691d15a7" :answer/id #uuid "f550b866-e3d0-5255-9950-2dbd691d15a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ec73c900-b909-5aa7-beeb-5f5b6ee2fba4" :question/id #uuid "ec73c900-b909-5aa7-beeb-5f5b6ee2fba4" :question/math-academy-id "q-141341" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $det(A)=0$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ we must have that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $det(A)=0.$* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then we must have $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$ * $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fb932edd-7a39-5566-85fa-5d17f1b76d5d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fb932edd-7a39-5566-85fa-5d17f1b76d5d" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb932edd-7a39-5566-85fa-5d17f1b76d5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a1868d1e-0ee5-5742-b6e3-4792cb79e39e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0d49a551-9ec5-52ad-a34a-89d55b7486b5" "answer-a1868d1e-0ee5-5742-b6e3-4792cb79e39e" "answer-662ea6db-c29f-5f39-b454-f93e28a4789e" "answer-41750c54-9a68-5140-acec-016759823bad" "answer-2487a691-60de-5d0e-a46b-689f90f253ca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d49a551-9ec5-52ad-a34a-89d55b7486b5" :answer/id #uuid "0d49a551-9ec5-52ad-a34a-89d55b7486b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1868d1e-0ee5-5742-b6e3-4792cb79e39e" :answer/id #uuid "a1868d1e-0ee5-5742-b6e3-4792cb79e39e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-662ea6db-c29f-5f39-b454-f93e28a4789e" :answer/id #uuid "662ea6db-c29f-5f39-b454-f93e28a4789e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41750c54-9a68-5140-acec-016759823bad" :answer/id #uuid "41750c54-9a68-5140-acec-016759823bad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2487a691-60de-5d0e-a46b-689f90f253ca" :answer/id #uuid "2487a691-60de-5d0e-a46b-689f90f253ca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a9326523-4bce-5554-9699-fb91223b9531" :question/id #uuid "a9326523-4bce-5554-9699-fb91223b9531" :question/math-academy-id "q-142479" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis\n\nIII. $det(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $A$ is invertible.* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$  then according to the invertible matrix theorem, $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis.* $\\,\\times $\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is *not* invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ which means that $\\text{Null}(A)$ actually has a basis.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $det(A)=0.$* $\\,✓$  \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is not invertible it must be $det(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1fa1830b-5add-5daf-9fd3-0b3e06eb4a22"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1fa1830b-5add-5daf-9fd3-0b3e06eb4a22" :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa1830b-5add-5daf-9fd3-0b3e06eb4a22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5fb3aa43-1e84-516c-8972-6a71a1a76857" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d9adf053-ad3b-5a09-87f7-674bd680f4dd" "answer-db451e16-e9ec-50a7-a360-3e56d95fe251" "answer-f36d2201-ba87-5be6-b825-8ab2db34fb07" "answer-bd0f6e35-d7c3-5c27-95f6-6b6b01493577" "answer-5fb3aa43-1e84-516c-8972-6a71a1a76857"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9adf053-ad3b-5a09-87f7-674bd680f4dd" :answer/id #uuid "d9adf053-ad3b-5a09-87f7-674bd680f4dd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db451e16-e9ec-50a7-a360-3e56d95fe251" :answer/id #uuid "db451e16-e9ec-50a7-a360-3e56d95fe251" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f36d2201-ba87-5be6-b825-8ab2db34fb07" :answer/id #uuid "f36d2201-ba87-5be6-b825-8ab2db34fb07" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd0f6e35-d7c3-5c27-95f6-6b6b01493577" :answer/id #uuid "bd0f6e35-d7c3-5c27-95f6-6b6b01493577" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fb3aa43-1e84-516c-8972-6a71a1a76857" :answer/id #uuid "5fb3aa43-1e84-516c-8972-6a71a1a76857" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186272349 :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\text{__________}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $det(A)=0$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}$\n\nIII. $A$ has $8$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $8\\times 8$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{8} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=8=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times $  \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}.$*  $\\,\\times $\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{8}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $A$ has $8$ pivot columns.* $\\,✓$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=8,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $8$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-833e6fc8-0df5-5faa-ab1e-b5f4126e71c3" :question/id #uuid "833e6fc8-0df5-5faa-ab1e-b5f4126e71c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-141215" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\text{__________}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $det(A)=0$\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)={R}^{6}$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6$" :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is an $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{6} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=6=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Null}(A)={R}^{6}.$* $\\,\\times $\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6.$* $\\,✓$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dd81b3b5-e497-5c05-9bc7-9bf55e4547fa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dd81b3b5-e497-5c05-9bc7-9bf55e4547fa" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd81b3b5-e497-5c05-9bc7-9bf55e4547fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6358e671-90b3-5914-a718-8213a1f17a31" :answer-field/choices ["answer-720f0040-8787-5886-9c1c-402554299b56" "answer-f701af70-1e73-5b6a-b0c6-4b6e59b2fa9c" "answer-65a82f6c-7a03-5152-b67b-6b75c8f2f8df" "answer-5ab377df-73df-53f2-81bc-0c28114d3720" "answer-6358e671-90b3-5914-a718-8213a1f17a31"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-720f0040-8787-5886-9c1c-402554299b56" :answer/id #uuid "720f0040-8787-5886-9c1c-402554299b56" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f701af70-1e73-5b6a-b0c6-4b6e59b2fa9c" :answer/id #uuid "f701af70-1e73-5b6a-b0c6-4b6e59b2fa9c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65a82f6c-7a03-5152-b67b-6b75c8f2f8df" :answer/id #uuid "65a82f6c-7a03-5152-b67b-6b75c8f2f8df" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ab377df-73df-53f2-81bc-0c28114d3720" :answer/id #uuid "5ab377df-73df-53f2-81bc-0c28114d3720" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6358e671-90b3-5914-a718-8213a1f17a31" :answer/id #uuid "6358e671-90b3-5914-a718-8213a1f17a31" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186348208 :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is **not** invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=n$\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is **not** invertible.* $\\,\\times $\n\nBy the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ we must have that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
